      "message": "Are you suggesting passing an `Option` to `process_request` instead?\n\nWhile that works for pvmfw as only supports protected VMs. It can raise an error when the DICE chain is missing and after it only handles the case with a valid DICE chain.\n\nFor rialto, since we aim to support both protected and non protected VMs, it would be more nature to use a sample DICE chain here than to create fake data at each usage point.\n\nOtherwise obtaining real data for non-protected VMs might not be straightforward. Since this functionality is intended for debugging purposes only for now, using a sample DICE chain is convenient in this scenario.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid_manager/src/dice.rs;l\u003d61;drc\u003d95084dfd8587992bb384759544678fd0ab5cef8b",
